Here is the Phase II logical data dictionary (docs/design/data_dictionary.md) for your Off-Grid Solar Micro-Grid Energy Billing & Battery Health Monitor project. In accordance with Phase II requirements, it lists each entity, key, relationship, column meaning, and required/unique status without Oracle data types or sizes.

Data Dictionary — Phase II Logical Design
Project: Off-Grid Solar Micro-Grid Energy Billing & Battery Health Monitor

Course: INSY 8311 & Database Development with PL/SQL

1. CUSTOMERS
Stores anonymised micro-grid customer records.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
customer_id	Unique internal identifier for an anonymised customer	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
customer_anon_code	External anonymised customer code from raw telemetry (e.g., CUST-1001)	Yes	Yes	Alternate Key
microgrid_zone	Standardised micro-grid service zone or cluster name	Yes	No	Attribute
account_status	Current customer status (e.g., active, suspended, inactive)	Yes	No	Attribute
registered_date	Date the customer account was onboarded to the micro-grid	Yes	No	Attribute
2. BATTERY_BANKS
Stores micro-grid battery bank hardware and capacity metadata.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
bank_id	Unique internal identifier for a battery bank	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
bank_code	External battery bank identifier from telemetry (e.g., BNK-10)	Yes	Yes	Alternate Key
microgrid_zone	Standardised micro-grid zone where the battery bank is installed	Yes	No	Attribute
nominal_capacity_kwh	Rated energy storage capacity of the battery bank	Yes	No	Attribute
bank_status	Operational status of the battery bank (e.g., normal, warning, maintenance)	Yes	No	Attribute
commissioned_date	Date the battery bank entered service	Yes	No	Attribute
3. METERS
Stores smart meter installations linked to customers and battery banks.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
meter_id	Unique internal identifier for a smart meter	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
meter_code	External smart meter identifier from raw data (e.g., MTR-200)	Yes	Yes	Alternate Key
customer_id	Customer to whom the smart meter is assigned	Yes	No	Foreign Key → CUSTOMERS.customer_id
bank_id	Battery bank supplying energy to the meter's zone/feeder	Yes	No	Foreign Key → BATTERY_BANKS.bank_id
meter_status	Current relay/connection state (e.g., active, disconnected)	Yes	No	Attribute
installed_date	Date the meter was installed	Yes	No	Attribute
4. PREPAID_ACCOUNTS
Stores prepaid energy balance and tariff terms per customer or meter account.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
account_id	Unique identifier for a prepaid energy account	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
customer_id	Owner of the prepaid account	Yes	No	Foreign Key → CUSTOMERS.customer_id
meter_id	Smart meter associated with the prepaid balance	Yes	Yes	Foreign Key → METERS.meter_id
current_balance	Current prepaid credit balance	Yes	No	Attribute
tariff_rate	Applicable energy unit rate for billing calculations	Yes	No	Attribute
last_updated_at	Timestamp when the balance or tariff was last updated	Yes	No	Attribute
5. ENERGY_TRANSACTIONS
Records prepaid credit top-ups and billing adjustments.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
transaction_id	Unique identifier for a billing or top-up transaction	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
account_id	Prepaid account affected by the transaction	Yes	No	Foreign Key → PREPAID_ACCOUNTS.account_id
meter_id	Smart meter associated with the transaction	Yes	No	Foreign Key → METERS.meter_id
transaction_type	Category of transaction (e.g., top-up, energy deduction, adjustment)	Yes	No	Attribute
amount	Monetary value of the transaction	Yes	No	Attribute
balance_after	Resulting prepaid balance after the transaction is recorded	Yes	No	Attribute
transaction_timestamp	Date and time when the transaction occurred	Yes	No	Attribute
6. CONSUMPTION_LOGS
Stores time-stamped energy usage readings captured from smart meters.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
consumption_id	Unique identifier for a consumption reading record	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
meter_id	Smart meter that reported the energy consumption	Yes	No	Foreign Key → METERS.meter_id
reading_timestamp	Date and time when the consumption reading was recorded	Yes	No	Attribute
energy_consumed	Energy used during the interval	Yes	No	Attribute
source_record_ref	Reference to the originating raw record identifier	No	No	Attribute
7. BATTERY_HEALTH_LOGS
Stores periodic electrical, thermal, and degradation telemetry for battery banks.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
health_log_id	Unique identifier for a battery telemetry snapshot	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
bank_id	Battery bank measured by the telemetry reading	Yes	No	Foreign Key → BATTERY_BANKS.bank_id
logged_timestamp	Date and time when telemetry was captured	Yes	No	Attribute
voltage	Measured battery bank voltage	Yes	No	Attribute
current	Measured charge/discharge current	Yes	No	Attribute
temperature	Measured battery temperature	Yes	No	Attribute
state_of_charge	State of Charge (SoC) percentage	Yes	No	Attribute
depth_of_discharge	Depth of Discharge (DoD) percentage	Yes	No	Attribute
state_of_health	State of Health (SoH) percentage	Yes	No	Attribute
charge_cycles	Cumulative charge/discharge cycle count	Yes	No	Attribute
8. MAINTENANCE_ALERTS
Tracks operational and battery warnings requiring operator or technician attention.

Column Name	Meaning	Required	Unique	Key / Reference
alert_id	Unique identifier for a maintenance or billing alert	Yes	Yes	Primary Key
bank_id	Related battery bank, if the alert stems from battery telemetry	No	No	Foreign Key → BATTERY_BANKS.bank_id
meter_id	Related smart meter, if the alert stems from meter status or credit	No	No	Foreign Key → METERS.meter_id
alert_category	Type of alert (e.g., low credit, disconnected meter, high temp, low SoH)	Yes	No	Attribute
severity_level	Urgency level of the alert (e.g., low, medium, high, critical)	Yes	No	Attribute
alert_status	Workflow state of the alert (e.g., open, acknowledged, resolved)	Yes	No	Attribute
triggered_at	Timestamp when the alert condition was detected	Yes	No	Attribute
resolved_at	Timestamp when the alert was resolved	No	No	Attribute
9. Summary of Logical Relationships (Crow's-Foot)
CUSTOMERS (1) to PREPAID_ACCOUNTS (0..N): A customer can hold one or more prepaid accounts.

CUSTOMERS (1) to METERS (0..N): A customer can have one or more assigned meters.

BATTERY_BANKS (1) to METERS (0..N): A battery bank can serve multiple smart meters.

PREPAID_ACCOUNTS (1) to ENERGY_TRANSACTIONS (0..N): A prepaid account accumulates top-up and billing transactions.

METERS (1) to CONSUMPTION_LOGS (0..N): A meter generates periodic energy consumption logs.

METERS (1) to ENERGY_TRANSACTIONS (0..N): Meter activity/top-ups link to transaction records.

BATTERY_BANKS (1) to BATTERY_HEALTH_LOGS (0..N): A battery bank records periodic health telemetry snapshots.

BATTERY_BANKS (0..1) to MAINTENANCE_ALERTS (0..N) and METERS (0..1) to MAINTENANCE_ALERTS (0..N): Alerts may reference a battery bank, a meter, or both depending on the trigger.

